    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family B). Stand-alone finding F40.C3 previously folded onto INV-bazij. Full evidence remains on INV-bazij's pass-40 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation as the **6th distinct INV-bazij mechanism**, joining the existing WI-bupim residual-cohort decomposition.\n\n## Symptom\n\nThe markdown analyzer's stable_id hash for internal-link kind nodes does not incorporate within-file occurrence index. When the same heading text appears multiple times in one file, the analyzer emits N identical-stable_id link nodes — one per occurrence.\n\nEvidence on `/tmp/p40_docs_bm.json` (DOCS substrate, 2861 nodes, 0.38% collision rate):\n- 11 colliding nodes; 4 distinct colliding stable_ids; all from one file: `adr/0013-structured-tracker.md`.\n- All colliders share the format `markdown:<path>:1411-1411:<heading>:link` — same line-range across collisions.\n- `## Key Design Decisions` appears 4× in the ADR (different sub-sections); each occurrence emits an identical-stable_id link node.\n- `Compile Rules` appears 3× and 2× in two other sub-locations of the same file.\n\nThis is the 6th distinct mechanism contributing to INV-bazij collision residual, structurally separate from prior cohorts:\n\n| # | Mechanism | Source analyzer | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | SQL parse-artifact | sql-linker | `SELECT users` 13× |\n| 2 | kafka-linker placeholder | kafka-linker | `kafka:publish:*` 5-8× |\n| 3 | bash export-VAR intrinsic | bash | `FORGEJO_TOKEN` within-name repetition |\n| 4 | HTTP-linker URL-variant collapse | http-linker | URL-variant collapse |\n| 5 | TypeScript hash-input-insufficient | js_ts | `{connect, connectWebSocket, registerServiceWorker, scheduleReconnect}` collapse to 1 stable_id |\n| **6** | **markdown within-file duplicate-heading** | **markdown** | **`## Key Design Decisions` 4× in adr/0013** |\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor markdown internal-link kind nodes, the stable_id hash must incorporate an occurrence index disambiguating multiple identical-text headings within the same file. After fix: distinct occurrences produce distinct stable_ids; collision residual on markdown-heavy substrates drops accordingly.\n\n## Cross-codebase impact\n\nDOCS substrate at 0.38% is below INV-bazij's 5% threshold so does NOT itself constitute a breach, but the within-file-dup-heading cohort contributes to ROOT 0.84% as residual masked by the large denominator. Mixed-content codebases that include ADRs, design docs, or any repeated-heading markdown will surface this cohort at proportionally higher rates.\n\n6-codebase INV-bazij matrix (snapshot from pass-40):\n\n| Codebase | Nodes | Rate | Dominant cohort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ROOT default | 34253 | 0.84% | mixed (this cohort masked) |\n| TRACKER | 4959 | 0.81% | python residual |\n| SCRIPTS default | 416 | 7.0% **BREACH** | bash export-VAR |\n| HTRAC | 77 | 16.88% **BREACH** | TS hash-input |\n| CLI_PKG | 32 | 0.00% | — |\n| DOCS default | 2861 | 0.38% | markdown within-file-dup-heading **NEW** |\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nExtend the markdown analyzer's stable_id hash input for internal-link kind to include an occurrence-index for the (file_path, heading_text) pair, computed at emission time. Equivalent fix-path family to WI-bupim's typed-tier name-disambiguation sweep, but specific to the markdown analyzer's hash construction site.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F40.C3** — INV-bazij discussion entry 2026-06-03T00:13:43 (pass-40 batch; full mechanism enumeration and 6-codebase matrix).\n\nLab notebook: pass 40 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-bazij** (META: stable_id mass collisions) — sibling row to WI-bupim under the same parent.\n- Sibling: **WI-bupim** (typed-tier stable_id name disambiguation — closely-analogous fix-path family but different analyzer surface).\n- Family B siblings: **WI-markdown-file-anchor-absent**, **WI-tier-classifier-markdown-coverage** (same subsystem, different surfaces)."  # 921f
    fields: {}  # 921f
