s` 4× in adr/0013** |\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor markdown internal-link kind nodes, the stable_id hash must incorporate an occurrence index disambiguating multiple identical-text headings within the same file. After fix: distinct occurrences produce distinct stable_ids; collision residual on markdown-heavy substrates drops accordingly.\n\n## Cross-codebase impact\n\nDOCS substrate at 0.38% is below INV-bazij's 5% threshold so does NOT itself constitute a breach, but the within-file-dup-heading cohort contributes to ROOT 0.84% as residual masked by the large denominator. Mixed-content codebases that include ADRs, design docs, or any repeated-heading markdown will surface this cohort at proportionally higher rates.\n\n6-codebase INV-bazij matrix (snapshot from pass-40):\n\n| Codebase | Nodes | Rate | Dominant cohort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ROOT default | 34253 | 0.84% | mixed (this cohort masked) |\n| TRACKER | 4959 | 0.81% | python residual |\n| SCRIPTS default | 416 | 7.0% **BREACH** | bash export-VAR |\n| HTRAC | 77 | 16.88% **BREACH** | TS hash-input |\n| CLI_PKG | 32 | 0.00% | — |\n| DOCS default | 2861 | 0.38% | markdown within-file-dup-heading **NEW** |\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nExtend the markdown analyzer's stable_id hash input for internal-link kind to include an occurrence-index for the (file_path, heading_text) pair, computed at emission time. Equivalent fix-path family to WI-bupim's typed-tier name-disambiguation sweep, but specific to the markdown analyzer's hash construction site.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F40.C3** — INV-bazij discussion entry 2026-06-03T00:13:43 (pass-40 batch; full mechanism enumeration and 6-codebase matrix).\n\nLab notebook: pass 40 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-bazij** (META: stable_id mass collisions) — sibling row to WI-bupim under the same parent.\n- Sibling: **WI-bupim** (typed-tier stable_id name disambiguation — closely-analogous fix-path family but different analyzer surface).\n- Family B siblings: **WI-markdown-file-anchor-absent**, **WI-tier-classifier-markdown-coverage** (same subsystem, different surfaces)."  # 2002
